      "message": "Not sure I understand your scenario. Maybe describe it step by step?\n\nIf your concern is the readNetworkStatsDetail will return an elapsedRealtime of previous function call. The answer is no because the native layer doesn\u0027t alter elapsedRealtime. So the elapsedRealtime of stats will be always generated by \"new NetworkStats(SystemClock.elapsedRealtime().\"\n\nIf your concern is \"this alter the behavior from get elapsedRealtime before  requestSwapActiveStatsMapLocked becomes get it after requestSwapActiveStatsMapLocked\", then yes.\nBut I don\u0027t think it really matters, because we are marking this result to this timestamp. Differs from few milliseconds doesn\u0027t really matters I think, since the NetworkStatsService only has the resolution of 2 hours. And this CL will not go to tm-dev, I think it is ok to monitor if it really causes problem?\n\nNot sure if this answers your question.",
